# sync_timedb startup day-close contract

When **`sync_startup_day_close_preflight=yes`** (default) **and CLI `startdate == 'all'`**, the supervisor starts a **single-flight** background discover thread (`sync_timedb.py [thread:startup-day-close-preflight]`). When **`sync_startup_tail_ingest_enabled=yes`** (opt-in; **default `no`**), a **pipelined** **`StartupTailIngestCoordinator`** thread (`[thread:startup-tail-ingest]`) consumes tail-eligible day enqueue from each discover slice. When **`sync_startup_drain_day_close_before_ingest=yes`**, the supervisor **blocks first rescan/ingest** until startup discover, startup tail ingest, startup raw-removal deletes, and day-close raw deletes that block startup are idle — **not** until all janitor **`DAY_CLOSE`** debt completes (one-time gate; **default is `no`** so ingest and archival start immediately). Date-range runs without **`all`** skip all startup preflights and the drain gate.

## Two-queue model (2026-06)

MainThread + pools own **ingest** (discover, handoff, chunk ingest, append dispatch, non-blocking day_close enqueue). **`ArchiveJanitor`** owns **archival** (proactive discover each tick, seal, verify, delete, tar drop on **`DAY_CLOSE`** debt). Chunk boundaries are **ingest-only**; steady-state delete never runs on the supervisor chunk loop. Full law: **`sync-timedb-archive-janitor-contract.mdc`**. Regression: **`test_arch_supervisor_chunk_loop_does_not_call_apply_batch_delete`**.

