## Coordination

- Janitor **`DAY_CLOSE`** debt submits to the same coordinator (no sync zstd on janitor thread). See **`sync-timedb-archive-janitor-contract.mdc`**.
- **`run_scheduled_maintenance_pass`** with `reason=startup` (heavy) or light passes runs **`_discover_and_enqueue_ready_day_close`** — not only log the candidate report. **No longer** triggered every `rescan_every_chunks` or on ingest-queue drain at chunk boundary (2026-06).

## Manifest-fast handoff (`phase=done`)

When per-day raw removal manifest **`phase=done`**, handoff eligibility (`should_handoff_to_ingest`, `handoff_paths_for_ingest`, `_only_waiting_on_ingest_blocks_completion`, `discover_manifest_handoffs`, **`closed_raw_paths_on_disk`**, **`discover_closed_raw_on_disk_handoffs`**, **`has_closed_raw_on_disk`**) uses **manifest + `os.path.isfile`** only — **no** nested `build_remaining_raw_stats_by_daily_gz` full collect. This avoids OOM/stall on large archives when async manifest is stuck at **`raw_delete_pending`** but verify already finished, and unblocks boot **`startup_closed_raw_handoff`** recovery (e.g. 05-22 with hundreds of retryable skips on disk).

**Handoff allowed when:** at least one manifest path exists on disk and every on-disk manifest entry is a retryable skip (not verified / pending delete).

**Tar drop (manifest/quarantine-aware):** `try_finish_tar_drop_if_ready`, async `_tar_drop_day` / `_day_close_filesystem_complete`, and janitor **`_close_one_day`** tar-drop steps use **`_remaining_raw_paths_blocking_tar_drop()`** (same truth as **`has_closed_raw_on_disk`**): quarantine-terminal manifest entries (`skipped_quarantine` / `reason=quarantine`) and **`get_quarantine_skip_paths()`** do **not** block `.tar` unlink when manifest is **`phase=done`**; stale janitor accrual alone must not block after manifest clean. Log **`sync_timedb: tar_drop_skip`** / **`tar_drop_deferred`** on skip. **`daily_tar_needs_day_close_work`** treats existing `.tar` as work when janitor hint ≥ `tar_dropped` (hint drift). See **`test_try_finish_tar_drop_manifest_done_stale_accrual`** / **`test_reopen_done_days_with_verified_on_disk_at_delete_pass_start`** in `test_sync_timedb_day_raw_removal.py`.

**Unmanifested closed raw** may still exist on disk; handoff requeues known retryable manifest paths and defers async — tar drop stays blocked until non-quarantine filesystem truth clears (see **`sync-timedb-db-before-archive-contract.mdc`**).

